# Derived by hand from Part III ch. 6 (`!Never` has one value, `never`, the event that never fires; a `match` on `Never` needs no arms): the request count and the last request stay as built, and only the pressed count moves.
test never_fires

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="press")
    1: Ui.Label(text="asked 0 times, last nothing; pressed 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="asked 0 times, last nothing; pressed 1")

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1: Ui.Label(text="asked 0 times, last nothing; pressed 2")
